  "verification": [
    "AFI identifies the production beach house on Westward Beach Road in Malibu; its Loophole entry corroborates that the same house was used in both films.",
    "The existing Movie Tourist film/now image pair shows the beach at the foot of cliffs, with the road above it, looking toward Point Dume. The source does not supply GPS coordinates.",
    "A local photo comparison places the now-vanished house on the beach between Sunset Restaurant and Point Dume cliffs. This is corroboration of the corridor only, not an independently surveyed parcel.",
    "The replacement point is an exact vertex on the official County CAMS Westward Beach Road centerline, well within that corridor. It is chosen as an honest approximation beside the historic beach scene, not as proof the house stood on the current road.",
    "USGS 1-metre elevation data for the replacement point gives 7.66 metres above reference elevation (June 2024 acquisition), whereas the old point gives -0.87 metres (2016 acquisition). Combined with the road geometry, this supports moving the display pin onto land. Coastal erosion means these data do not establish today’s beach width."
  ],
